//api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101398","id":3947461220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rSXpk","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T21:36:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T21:36:13Z","body":"I think it is just a matter of making the selection bigger internally when  `centerX=centerY=CenterZ=false` so that it includes what’s on the edges.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3947461220/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3947579494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101398#issuecomment-3947579494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101398","id":3947579494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rS0hm","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T22:04:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T22:04:01Z","body":"Isn't that a naive approach? It would make possible for the selection to pick unwanted cells, and it just becomes a different problem.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3947579494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3947766169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101398#issuecomment-3947766169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101398","id":3947766169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rTiGZ","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T22:46:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T22:46:26Z","body":"This is not so naive, it is simply a correction for the misalignment.\n\n I need to check the specific (which corner) but this is just how the selection is coded, it tracks the start and end cubes. When the grid is not centered, it means it tracks a corner of these cubes, which means it won't include the opposite corner and edges. Hence you need to add +1 to be inclusive.\n\nI will try to draw that tomorrow so that it's clearer. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3947766169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3962150331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101398#issuecomment-3962150331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101398","id":3962150331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sKZ27","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T21:19:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T21:26:06Z","body":"Here are the much awaited drawings 😃 \n\nHere the difference between Center X = Center Y = Center Z being true or false:\n\n<img width=\"947\" height=\"429\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c106565-c9d1-4ebd-821a-91007cbdc582\" />\n\nAnd here is the problem it causes with the selection, and why we just need to add +1:\n\n<img width=\"1129\" height=\"358\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1f1ec13c-0355-445c-bf35-7f87a9a7b269\" />\n\nThe blue rectangle represents the selection box, with the start and end cube coordinates - in cell coordinates. The blue dots are representing what is being selected in point coordinates.\n\nYou can see that if we just use the cell coordinates as point coordinates, we end up selecting the assets on the top and left edges of the selection, but not the assets on the right and bottom edges of the selection.\n\nIf we add +1 to the end cube coordinate, we implement a \"include edges\" selection, if we substract -1 to the start cube, we implement a \"exclude edges\" selection.\n\n**NOTE:** if CenterX = false and CenterY=CenterZ=true, then you would only add +1 to the X coordinate of the end selection cube to implement \"include edges\". \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3962150331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]